  "answer": "I'll look through the diagnosing skill and the product special-price path so we can see why an end date hides the discount.The discount check compares the start date with itself, so a special that has an end date never becomes active. I'll correct that comparison and lock it in with a test.The storefront price calculation in `ProductPriceUtils` treated a dated special as active only when the start date was both before and after the current time, so any special with an end date was ignored. It now applies the special amount when the start date, if present, has been reached and the end date is still today or later, counting the end date as a full calendar day. Specials with no dates are unchanged.\n\nVERIFICATION: {\"ran\": [\"mvn -pl sm-core -am test -Dtest=ProductPriceUtilsSpecialTest -DfailIfNoTests=false\"], \"result\": \"passed\", \"could_not_verify\": [\"storefront HTTP API against a running Shopizer server\"], \"missing\": [\"an existing product-price test fixture in the repo\"]}",
